    "gaps": [
      "Fixed source registry and alias specialization; arbitrary registry overrides are outside this contract.",
      "Leaf internals remain inside visit; subprocess JSON is captured stdout, not a separately typed planning artifact.",
      "Lunar enforces workflow call and wall budgets and records receipts. The native child has no configured subprocess timeout; source optional reporting remains caller-owned."
    ]
  },
  "extensions": {
    "mathformer.source": {
      "category": "hub",
      "native_id": "physics-lib:coherence-repair-plan",
      "owner_skill": "skills/control/workflow-contract-validator/SKILL.md",
      "contract": {
        "id": "physics-lib:coherence-repair-plan",
        "summary": "Alias for MathformerPhysicsLib coherence repair planning.",
        "family": "mathformerphysicslib",
        "kind": "sequence",
        "safety": "read_only",
        "command": [],
        "depends_on": [
          "mathformerphysicslib:coherence-repair-plan"
        ],
        "writes": [],
        "allows_extra_args": false,
        "timeout_seconds": null
      }
    },
    "mathformer.native_boundary": {
      "execution": "Registered MCP tools call shared scripts/mathformer.py stages; visit recurses through the native controller and registered planner subprocess with the explicit repository_root mount.",
      "failure_policy": "Preserve native failure payloads; only operation exceptions terminate graph execution.",
      "scientific_payloads": "HubResult is a transport envelope; repair_required still permits exit zero.",
      "transport": "Lunar requires a top-level bounded loop. Rejected admission is carried through it without visiting dependencies; admitted work retains source ordering and state."
    },
    "mathformer.composition": {
      "ordered_dependencies": [
        "mathformerphysicslib:coherence-repair-plan"
      ],
      "dependency_workflows": [
        "hub_mathformerphysicslib_coherence_repair_plan_workflow"
      ],
      "command_after_dependencies": false,
      "keep_going_semantics": "Sticky failure; no further work exists after the only child.",
      "extra_args_for_sequence": "rejected by run_action",
      "bound_semantics": "Exactly one visit sets done=true; source returns normally at this bound. Exhaustion failure is unreachable.",
      "callers": "Hub CLI/NL dispatch; repair_plan is also reused by MCP ports, coherence gate and coherence-loop reporting."
    },
    "mathformer.steps": {
      "admit": "scripts/mathformer.py:build_registry, admit_action. Use the source registry and fixed physics-lib:coherence-repair-plan identity. Copy seen; check unknown action, then cycle, then add identity and reject extra_args for sequences. Return accepted, status and sorted ancestry.",
      "reject": "scripts/mathformer.py:reject_action. Return ok=false, admission status and fixed action_id; add sorted cycle for dependency_cycle.",
      "initialize": "scripts/mathformer.py:initialize_dependencies. Pack index=0, children=[], dependencies_ok=true and copied ancestry.",
      "visit": "scripts/mathformer.py:visit_dependency, run_action, run_leaf_action. Select depends_on[state.index]; recurse with ancestry, context and the same repository mount, forwarding no extra arguments. Child admission precedes preflight; errors return failure, dry-run returns without launching. Otherwise snapshot, launch the registered planner with --self-test --json, capture stdout/stderr/returncode, then audit writes. Nonzero exit or unexpected writes set ok=false; launch errors propagate. plan_coherence_repairs.py:main loads explicit reports or default_reports; defaults select self_test_payload or build_inventory, then canonicalize, audit_grounding, critic_redefinitions, critic_integration, critic_api in order. This registration selects self-test, supplies no reports/output, and passes the aggregate self-test result into canonicalize as inventory; do not substitute self_test_inventory. coherence_common.py:repair_plan traverses reports then findings, carrying append-only actions; every finding appends exactly one action. Owner conflicts/spread select consolidate_concept_owner; integration gaps select repair_integration_surface; absent/thin API selects add_operable_bridge_api; other kinds select record_or_block_gap. It returns repair_required if actions exist, otherwise no_repairs_required. Main optionally writes output, emits JSON and returns zero for either planning status; exceptions propagate to subprocess failure. Helper loops/logs/timing/audits stay here.",
      "advance": "scripts/mathformer.py:advance_dependencies. Increment index, append child once, preserve ancestry, and set dependencies_ok to previous dependencies_ok AND bool(child.get(\"ok\", false)). Compute done as index == len(depends_on) OR (NOT child.ok AND NOT context.keep_going). For this one-child alias, exhaustion is true after the first visit even with keep_going.",
      "finish": "scripts/mathformer.py:dependency_command_guard, finish_dependencies, prepare_action, run_action. The alias command is empty, so its command guard is always false. Return action metadata, children, sticky ok, and sequence_completed or sequence_failed; run_action returns this result immediately. Never launch a parent command or execute repairs.",
      "carry": "Transport only: carry rejection and unchanged inert state through the top-level Lunar loop; no native operation or side effect."
    }
  }
}
